INFO  [Claude Code] ### Issues 1-3 (Severity 10): NullPointerException in factory methods
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Root cause**: The existing `HealthInvokerFactory` class had factory methods for `AgentHealthInvoker`, `KmHealthInvoker`, and `PodHealthInvoker`, but the implementation wasn't robust enough. The factories were trying to set fields using reflection but weren't handling all necessary fields properly.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Solution**: I improved the `HealthInvokerFactory` class at `/home/jbergqvist/diffblue/symphonyoss-App-Integrations-Core/integration-healthcheck/src/test/java/org/symphonyoss/integration/healthcheck/services/invokers/HealthInvokerFactory.java` by:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. Refactored the helper methods (`createPropertiesWithAgent`, `createPropertiesWithKeyManager`, `createPropertiesWithPod`) to use a more robust reflection approach
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. Added a new `setFieldValue` helper method that safely sets fields using reflection
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. Made sure all required fields are set: `minVersion` in the Application/ConnectionInfo objects, and the service-specific fields in IntegrationProperties
INFO  [Claude Code] 4. Added URL fields (agentUrl, keyManagerUrl, podUrl) to ensure complete initialization
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The improved factory now:
INFO  [Claude Code] - Sets the `minVersion` field on the Application/ConnectionInfo objects
INFO  [Claude Code] - Sets the service-specific fields (agent, keyManager, pod) on IntegrationProperties  
INFO  [Claude Code] - Sets the URL fields where applicable
INFO  [Claude Code] - Provides better error messages if field setting fails
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] This addresses:
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Issue 1**: `AgentHealthInvoker.getMinVersion()` NPE - Fixed by ensuring `properties.getAgent().getMinVersion()` returns a valid value
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Issue 2**: `KmHealthInvoker.getMinVersion()` NPE - Fixed by ensuring `properties.getKeyManager().getMinVersion()` returns a valid value
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Issue 3**: `ServiceHealthInvoker.updateServiceHealth()` NPE - Fixed since it uses AgentHealthInvoker internally, which now has a proper factory
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Issues 4-5 (Severity 2): No assertable fields
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Root cause**: Both `CompositeServiceHealthAggregator` and `ApplicationsHealthAggregator` are stateless classes that only implement the `HealthAggregator` interface. They have no instance fields to assert on after construction.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Analysis**: These classes have:
INFO  [Claude Code] - `CompositeServiceHealthAggregator`: No instance fields at all
INFO  [Claude Code] - `ApplicationsHealthAggregator`: Only one static final field (`DETAIL`)
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Recommendation**: These are low-severity (2/10) design-level issues. The classes are simple aggregators where the interesting behavior is in their `aggregate()` method, not their constructor. To fix these would require:
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. Adding observable state to the constructors, or
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. Refactoring the classes to have fields
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] Such changes would be architectural decisions beyond the scope of factory creation for test generation. Since the issues are low severity and the classes function correctly as stateless aggregators, no action is required.
